{"chunk_id":"R4-2603988-001","collection":"ran4_tdoc_chunks","metadata":{"source":["CATT"],"tdocNumber":"R4-2603988","title":"Further discussion on 6G RF specs improvement"},"point_id":"10411399242325045878"}
The lack of a clear and consolidated view of how individual features impact RF requirements may lead to inconsistencies, overlooked impacts, or incomplete CRs when introducing or modifying features. To address this, one possible way is to introduce a sub-clause within RF specifications where a centralized table is created to explicitly map each feature to its associated RF requirements. Such a table would provide a structured overview, indicating which RF parameters, test cases, and performance requirements are affected by a given feature. The centralized table could include, for example: A list of features (e.g., CA, MIMO, MPR enhancement etc.) References to the impacted RF requirements (e.g., clauses, tables, or test specifications) Optional notes indicating the nature of the impact (e.g., new requirement, modified limit, conditional applicability) By providing a single point of reference, this approach would improve transparency and traceability of feature impacts across the specifications. It would also support more efficient CR drafting and review, reduce the risk of missing related updates, and facilitate a more consistent and maintainable specification structure. Overall, the introduction of such a centralized mapping table is expected to enhance both the usability and quality of RF specifications. Proposal: RAN4 to consider introducing a sub-clause within RF specifications where a centralized table is created to explicitly map each feature to its associated RF requirements in order to provide a structured overview. In this contribution, we have the following proposal on 6G RF specs improvement: Proposal: RAN4 to consider introducing a sub-clause within RF specifications where a centralized table is created to explicitly map each feature to its associated RF requirements in order to provide a structured overview. [1] R4-2602153, “Topic summary for [118][111] 6G operation efficiency”, Feature Lead (CATT) [2] R4-2602258, “Way forward for [118][111] 6G operation efficiency”, Feature Lead (CATT)

